    {
      "id": "W1RBIXU2VdC59_R_RJKGH",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -894.286302100241,
      "y": -156.05771367862008,
      "width": 934.1193237304688,
      "height": 150,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b5G",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1349655869,
      "version": 361,
      "versionNonce": 2107850291,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1785691509442,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Read scaling follow natural progression from simple optimization to complex distributed systems\n1. optimize read performance within DB\n2. scale DB horizontally \n3. add external caching layers\n\n",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Read scaling follow natural progression from simple optimization to complex distributed systems\n1. optimize read performance within DB\n2. scale DB horizontally \n3. add external caching layers\n\n",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "twWgDqIs9pDFopKyGR6v7",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -897.5739827417775,
      "y": -27.838856056054453,
      "width": 968.4393310546875,
      "height": 475,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b5H",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1799082621,
      "version": 736,
      "versionNonce": 1479512947,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1785691527610,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Optimize DB\n** Indexing:\n- When you query without an index, the database performs what's called a full table scan, \nit reads every single row to find matches. With an index, it can jump directly to the relevant rows. \nThis turns a linear O(n) operation into a logarithmic O(log n) operation, which is the difference \nbetween scanning 1 million rows versus checking maybe 20 index entries.\nType of DB indexing:\n1) B-tree Indexes (default)\n2) LSM tree (log structured merged tree)\n3) Hash indexes\n4) Geospatial indexes\n5) Inverted indexes\n\n\nOptimization patterns:\n1) Composite indexes: order of the key matter,\nand can help expensive sort\n\n",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Optimize DB\n** Indexing:\n- When you query without an index, the database performs what's called a full table scan, \nit reads every single row to find matches. With an index, it can jump directly to the relevant rows. \nThis turns a linear O(n) operation into a logarithmic O(log n) operation, which is the difference \nbetween scanning 1 million rows versus checking maybe 20 index entries.\nType of DB indexing:\n1) B-tree Indexes (default)\n2) LSM tree (log structured merged tree)\n3) Hash indexes\n4) Geospatial indexes\n5) Inverted indexes\n\n\nOptimization patterns:\n1) Composite indexes: order of the key matter,\nand can help expensive sort\n\n",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
